# BUG-260811-3qdo3e outcome

## Reproduction and corrected root cause

The first implementation removed two sequential `sleep 2` channels from the exact caller-cancellation test and replaced them with one deterministic EOF-driven `cat` channel. That change preserved the scoped-cancellation and no-implicit-idle-timeout assertions and reduced the exact case from about 4.1 seconds to about 0.2 seconds, but independent aggregate review found a second lifecycle cycle.

After 15 clean unfiltered runs, reviewer run 16 remained live beyond 90 seconds. `swift-inspect dump-concurrency` identified `automaticKeepaliveSurvivesLongRekey`: the test caller was in `LibSSH2Transport.close -> tearDown -> Task.value`, the cancelled automatic keepalive was in `sendKeepalive -> handleOperationFailure -> tearDown`, and teardown was draining the transport-owned automatic task. The keepalive therefore awaited teardown while teardown awaited that same keepalive. A `LibSSH2TimeoutRace` timer was also suspended in `ManualFixtureClock.sleep`, so the injected clock exposed the self-join without an independently advancing teardown deadline. The review-created listener PID 27811 was cleaned after sampling.

## Fix

The keepalive path now uses the same ownership rule already established for automatic rekey:

- public `sendKeepalive()` callers still wait for fatal teardown;
- the transport-owned automatic keepalive starts fatal teardown without awaiting it;
- the automatic keepalive then returns through its failure handler, allowing teardown to drain it normally.

A real-sshd Swift Testing regression advances `ManualFixtureClock` into an automatic keepalive, injects a socket failure, and requires the transport to reach `.closed` with `ownedResourceSnapshot() == .zero`. The positive long-rekey keepalive case remains intact. No skip, sleep-only workaround, wall-clock timeout mask, shorter timeout, or security-policy change was added.

The repaired exact cancellation test still proves that advancing the manual clock leaves an idle read pending, caller cancellation returns `cancelled` for the exact channel with `sameChannelOperation` and `requiresTeardown == false`, the same channel remains usable after cancellation, a sibling exec remains usable, and final owned resources are zero.

## Before/after and resource cleanup

- Before: the original exact test took 4.116-4.154 seconds and aggregate attempts appeared to stop around its reporting position; the first repair made it deterministic but independent run 16 exposed the automatic-keepalive self-join after 15 clean 426-test runs.
- After: the exact case passed 30 consecutive focused invocations; the positive automatic-keepalive/rekey case and the new fatal automatic-keepalive teardown case both passed; the complete real-sshd integration suite passed 25 tests.
- After: the first 20 consecutive unfiltered `swift test --skip-build` invocations passed 427 tests in 35 suites with exit 0. After the regression's scheduling assertions were made bounded, a final reset-on-any-failure gate again completed 20/20 consecutive final-tree invocations with 427 tests in 35 suites and exit 0. Runs 13 and 16, the two known hang positions, completed normally. Final-gate durations were 17-19 seconds.
- Resource baseline: sshd listener PIDs 1330 and 34815 predated this validation. The post-streak listener set was identical; this run leaked no sshd listener.
- Logs: `.temp/BUG-260811-3qdo3e/focused-cancellation-after-fix-01.log` through `-30.log`; the first unfiltered streak is `unfiltered-after-fix-01.log` through `-20.log`; the final-tree streak is `consecutive-gate-001.log` through `-020.log`.

Two later exploratory streaks were explicitly discarded before the final gate. `final-unfiltered-19.log` contains one unrelated `PacketFlowBridgeBoundedTests.reverseTimeBudget` fake-clock counter issue (expected 2, observed 1); that exact case immediately passed focused with exit 0. `final-streak-retry-10.log` contains a pre-existing `concurrentSameChannelWrites` test race where EOF reached a writer before actor admission and the writer correctly returned `writeAfterEOF`. The repaired cancellation test, both automatic-keepalive tests, and the LibSSH suite portions relevant to this bug passed in those runs. Neither discarded failure was counted toward the final streak, and neither out-of-scope test was weakened or changed.

## Retained TASK-260715-1u2vpc work

The uncommitted approved-algorithm matrix remains present: `approvedAlgorithmCompatibilityMatrix`, `assertApprovedAlgorithmCompatibility`, algorithm-configurable `LoopbackSSHD`, and the configurable KEX/host-key/cipher/MAC fixture inputs were not reverted, stashed, or rewritten.

